{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 17: one stock, two loops. Service contracts won by references from existing contracts (R1) and lost faster as contracts crowd a fixed service capacity (B1). }
Win Rate=
	0.2
	~	1/month
	~	New contracts won per month per existing contract, through references.
	|
Service Capacity=
	1000
	~	contracts
	~	Contracts the service team can hold before crowding drives losses up to the win rate.
	|
Contract Wins=
	Contracts * Win Rate
	~	contracts/month
	~	|
Contract Losses=
	Contracts * Win Rate * Contracts / Service Capacity
	~	contracts/month
	~	Losses rise with crowding: each contract's loss rate grows with the share of capacity in use.
	|
Contracts= INTEG(
	Contract Wins - Contract Losses,
	50)
	~	contracts
	~	|
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ month ~ |
FINAL TIME = 48 ~ month ~ |
TIME STEP = 0.0625 ~ month ~ |
SAVEPER = 0.0625 ~ month ~ |
